h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H1476","lemma":"גּוּנִי","tr":"gu·ni","gloss":"Guni","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H5548","lemma":"סַלְכָה","tr":"sal·khah","gloss":"Salecah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7218","lemma":"רֹאשׁ","tr":"rosh","gloss":"head","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":599},{"base":"H0032","lemma":"אֲבִיחַ֫יִל","tr":"a·vi·ha·yil","gloss":"Abihail","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H8289","lemma":"שָׁרוֹן","tr":"sha·ron","gloss":"Lasharon","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":13,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"also Gilead and the territory of the Geshurites and Maacathites, all of Mount Hermon, and all Bashan as far as Salecah—","from":11},{"book":"2KI","chapter":14,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Jehoash rested with his fathers and was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel. And his son Jeroboam reigned in his place.","from":17},{"book":"2KI","chapter":14,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"As for the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, along with all his accomplishments and might, and how he waged war and recovered both Damascus and Hamath for Israel from Judah, are they not written in the Book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel?","from":17},{"book":"2KI","chapter":15,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"In the second year of the reign of Pekah son of Remaliah over Israel, Jotham son of Uzziah became king of Judah.","from":17},{"book":"1CH","chapter":27,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Shitrai the Sharonite was in charge of the herds grazing in Sharon. Shaphat son of Adlai was in charge of the herds in the valleys.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":22,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Uz the firstborn, his brother Buz, Kemuel (the father of Aram),","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Leah said, “How fortunate!” So she named him Gad.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":31,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So he took his relatives with him, pursued Jacob for seven days, and overtook him in the hill country of Gilead.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"18-22":{"people":[{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"hagri-h1905","name":"Hagri","kind":"person","brief":"David's warrior","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"kedemah-h6929","name":"Kedemah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Ishmael","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"naphish-h5305","name":"Naphish","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Ishmael","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"places":[{"id":"jetur-h3195h","name":"Jetur","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"words":[{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":506},{"base":"H4421","lemma":"מִלְחָמָה","tr":"mil·cha·mah","gloss":"battle","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":319},{"base":"H1905","lemma":"הַגְרִי","tr":"hag·ri","gloss":"Hagri","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H3967","lemma":"מֵאָה","tr":"me·ah","gloss":"hundred","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":581},{"base":"H2572","lemma":"חֲמִשִּׁים","tr":"cha·mish·shim","gloss":"fifty","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":163},{"base":"H3195","lemma":"יְטוּר","tr":"ye·tur","gloss":"Jetur","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H5305","lemma":"נָפִישׁ","tr":"na·phish","gloss":"Naphish","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H1425","lemma":"גָּדִי","tr":"ga·di","gloss":"Gad","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1051},{"base":"H6279","lemma":"עָתַר","tr":"a·tar","gloss":"to pray","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":22,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"In You our fathers trusted; they trusted and You delivered them.","from":20},{"book":"PSA","chapter":22,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"They cried out to You and were set free; they trusted in You and were not disappointed.","from":20},{"book":"PSA","chapter":9,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Those who know Your name trust in You, for You, O LORD, have not forsaken those who seek You.","from":20},{"book":"2CH","chapter":18,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"When the chariot commanders saw Jehoshaphat, they said, “This is the king of Israel!” So they turned to fight against him, but Jehoshaphat cried out, and the LORD helped him. God drew them away from him.","from":20},{"book":"PSA","chapter":20,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"Some trust in chariots and others in horses, but we trust in the name of the LORD our God.","from":20},{"book":"PSA","chapter":20,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"They collapse and fall, but we rise up and stand firm.","from":20},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"There has been no day like it before or since, when the LORD listened to the voice of a man, because the LORD fought for Israel.","from":20},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"And because the LORD, the God of Israel, fought for Israel, Joshua captured all these kings and their land in one campaign.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"23-26":{"people":[{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"azriel-h5837g","name":"Azriel","kind":"person","brief":"Manasseh leader","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"eliel-h0447g","name":"Eliel","kind":"person","brief":"From Manasseh","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"epher-h6081i","name":"Epher","kind":"person","brief":"Manasseh leader","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"hodaviah-h1938h","name":"Hodaviah","kind":"person","brief":"Manasseh leader","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"ishi-h3469j","name":"Ishi","kind":"person","brief":"Manasseh leader","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"jahdiel-h3164","name":"Jahdiel","kind":"person","brief":"Manasseh leader","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"jeremiah-h3414h","name":"Jeremiah","kind":"person","brief":"Manasseh leader","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"tiglath-pileser-h8407","name":"Tiglath-pileser","kind":"person","brief":"Assyrian king","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"places":[{"id":"bashan-h1316","name":"Bashan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"hermon-mount-h2768","name":"Hermon Mount","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"assyria-h0804g","name":"Assyria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"gozan-h1470","name":"Gozan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"habor-h2249","name":"Habor","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"halah-h2477","name":"Halah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"hara-h2024","name":"Hara","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"words":[{"base":"H1179","lemma":"בַּ֫עַל חֶרְמוֹן","tr":"ba·al cher·mon","gloss":"(Mount) Baal-hermon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H8407","lemma":"תִּגְלַת פִּלְאֶ֫סֶר","tr":"tig·lat pil·e·ser","gloss":"Tiglath-pileser","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H2677","lemma":"חֲצִי","tr":"che·tsi","gloss":"half","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":125},{"base":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","tr":"me·nash·sheh","gloss":"Manasseh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":146},{"base":"H0804","lemma":"אַשּׁוּר","tr":"ash·shur","gloss":"Assyria","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":151},{"base":"H7626","lemma":"שֵׁ֫בֶט","tr":"she·vet","gloss":"tribe: staff","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":190},{"base":"H7307","lemma":"רוּחַ","tr":"ru·ach","gloss":"spirit","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":378},{"base":"H2249","lemma":"חָבוֹר","tr":"cha·vor","gloss":"Habor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H2477","lemma":"חֲלַח","tr":"cha·lach","gloss":"Halah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H5837","lemma":"עַזְרִיאֵל","tr":"az·ri·el","gloss":"Azriel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":15,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Then Pul king of Assyria invaded the land, and Menahem gave Pul a thousand talents of silver in order to gain his support and strengthen his own grip on the kingdom.","from":26},{"book":"2KI","chapter":17,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"In the ninth year of Hoshea, the king of Assyria captured Samaria and carried away the Israelites to Assyria, where he settled them in Halah, in Gozan by the Habor River, and in the cities of the Medes.","from":26},{"book":"2KI","chapter":15,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"In the days of Pekah king of Israel, Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria came and captured Ijon, Abel-beth-maacah, Janoah, Kedesh, Hazor, Gilead, and Galilee, including all the land of Naphtali, and he took the people as captives to Assyria.","from":26},{"book":"2KI","chapter":18,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The king of Assyria exiled the Israelites to Assyria and settled them in Halah, in Gozan by the Habor River, and in the cities of the Medes.","from":26},{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"and Beerah his son, whom Tiglath-pileser king of Assyria carried into exile. Beerah was a leader of the Reubenites.","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":34,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Do not make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, for when they prostitute themselves to their gods and sacrifice to them, they will invite you, and you will eat their sacrifices.","from":25},{"book":"JOS","chapter":13,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"also Gilead and the territory of the Geshurites and Maacathites, all of Mount Hermon, and all Bashan as far as Salecah—","from":23},{"book":"JOS","chapter":13,"verse":29,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"This is what Moses had given to the clans of the half-tribe of Manasseh, that is, to half the tribe of the descendants of Manasseh: The territory from Mahanaim through all Bashan—all the kingdom of Og king of Bashan, including all the towns of Jair that are in Bashan, sixty cities; half of Gilead; and Ashtaroth and Edrei, the royal cities of Og in Bashan. All this was for the clans of the descendants of Machir son of Manasseh, that is, half of the descendants of Machir.","from":23}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}